<article class="env-definition" id="03KZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03KZ">Definition <span data-tag="03KZ">68.17.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. We say an algebraic space $X$ over $S$ <em>has property $(\beta )$</em> if $X$ has the corresponding property of Lemma <a href="/tag/03JX" data-tag="03JX">68.5.1</a>. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
We say $f$ <em>has property $(\beta )$</em> if for any scheme $T$ and morphism $T \to Y$ the fibre product $T \times _ Y X$ has property $(\beta )$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $f$ is <em>decent</em> if for any scheme $T$ and morphism $T \to Y$ the fibre product $T \times _ Y X$ is a decent algebraic space. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $f$ is <em>reasonable</em> if for any scheme $T$ and morphism $T \to Y$ the fibre product $T \times _ Y X$ is a reasonable algebraic space. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $f$ is <em>very reasonable</em> if for any scheme $T$ and morphism $T \to Y$ the fibre product $T \times _ Y X$ is a very reasonable algebraic space. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>